Aim:
To create an Amazon EC2 instance, configure a web server, and associate an Elastic IP address with the instance.
Procedure:
Step 1: Login to AWS Management Console
1. Open a browser and go to https://aws.amazon.com
2. Click Sign In to the Console.
3. Login using AWS credentials.
Step 2: Launch an EC2 Instance
1. In AWS Console, search for EC2.
2. Click EC2 → Instances → Launch Instance.
3. Enter Instance Name: Webserver-EC2
Step 3: Choose Amazon Machine Image (AMI)
1. Select Amazon Linux 2 AMI (Free tier eligible).
2. Click Select.
Step 4: Choose Instance Type
1. Select t2.micro (Free tier eligible).
2. Click Next.
Step 5: Create Key Pair
1. Click Create new key pair.
2. Key pair name: webkey
3. Key type: RSA
4. Download and save the .pem file.
5. Click Continue.
Step 6: Configure Security Group
1. Create a new security group.
2. Security group name: webserver
3. Add rules as shown below:
Type	Protocol	Port	Source
SSH	TCP	22	My IP
HTTP	TCP	80	Anywhere (0.0.0.0/0)

This allows web traffic on port 80.

Step 7: Launch the Instance
1. Review the settings.
2. Click Launch Instance.
3. Wait until the instance state becomes Running.
Step 8: Associate Public IP Address
1. EC2 automatically assigns a public IPv4 address.
2. Copy the public IP or Public DNS.
Step 9: Connect to EC2 Instance
1. Select the instance.
2. Click Connect.
3. Choose EC2 Instance Connect.
4. Click Connect.
Step 10: Install Web Server (Apache)

Run the following commands in the terminal:
sudo yum update -y
sudo yum install httpd -y
sudo systemctl start httpd
sudo systemctl enable httpd


Step 11: Create a Sample Web Page

Run:
cd /var/www/html
sudo nano index.html


Add the following code:
<html>
<head>
    <title>EC2 Web Server</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Welcome to Amazon EC2 Web Server</h1>
    <p>Web server successfully running on EC2 instance</p>
</body>
</html>


Save and exit.

Step 12: Access the Web Server
1. Open a browser.
2. Enter:
http://<Public-IP-Address>


Example:
http://13.235.xxx.xxx
